[
    {
        "content": "<p>The <code>inversion</code> tactic seems very useful when doing Coq proofs about inductive predicates.<br>\nI wonder if there is a version of this tactic implemented in lean ?</p>\n<p>There are people in my lab working on _small_ inversions which seems a little simpler to implement but I lack some knowledge about metaprogramming before attempting to do so.</p>\n<p>Is there people working on this already ?</p>",
        "id": 455145797,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Vigouroux",
        "timestamp": 1722351764
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>cases</code> does inversion for you</p>",
        "id": 455145992,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1722351830
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hmmm<br>\nI have a Coq proof that I am attempting to reproduce, but for some reason cases does not help me...</p>",
        "id": 455146423,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Vigouroux",
        "timestamp": 1722351946
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What does this tactic do in Coq?</p>",
        "id": 455149002,
        "sender_full_name": "Yury G. Kudryashov",
        "timestamp": 1722352712
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's used when you have some <code>h : InductivePredicate a b c</code> and you want to do <code>cases h</code> to show that <code>a</code> <code>b</code> and <code>c</code> are of a certain form + some additional assumptions (potentially in multiple cases).</p>",
        "id": 455150533,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1722353200
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"658705\">@Thomas Vigouroux</span> Do you have an <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> for the case when <code>inversion</code> works but <code>cases</code> fails?</p>",
        "id": 455153586,
        "sender_full_name": "Yury G. Kudryashov",
        "timestamp": 1722354200
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Unfortunately not, the example I have is very big<br>\nI'll try a to find a different formulation of my inductive to see if that helps</p>",
        "id": 455153913,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Vigouroux",
        "timestamp": 1722354316
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>what is the error message?</p>",
        "id": 455194079,
        "sender_full_name": "Mario Carneiro",
        "timestamp": 1722365278
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I hope y'all don't mind I revive this thread, I happen to be comparing some Rocq proofs against Lean proofs and came across the same question<br>\nHere's my example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- cases le /- Dependent elimination failed: Failed to solve equation 0 = f n -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">generalize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">contradiction</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In Rocq, it would suffice to invoke <code>inversion le</code> directly, since it generalizes the indices of <code>le</code> automatically, and it also handles the contradictory case on its own because tries to unify the generalized variables after inversion. Is there any particular reason a corresponding Lean tactic doesn't exist? If I were to implement such a tactic, would there be interest in including it in a community library like mathlib or batteries?</p>",
        "id": 582893736,
        "sender_full_name": "Jonathan Chan",
        "timestamp": 1774989860
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just to clarify, if you replace <code>f n</code> with just <code>n</code>, <code>cases le</code> already generalizes the indices of <code>le</code>, applies the case splitting primitive and substitutes the equalities that come from generalization, discharging contradictory cases in the process. The problem here is the substitution step: While an equality like <code>n = 0</code> or maybe even <code>n + 1 = 1</code> is easy enough to substitute, you can't easily subsitute an equality <code>f n = 0</code> without losing information, and not substituting would leave behind additional, \"unexpected\" hypotheses; both of these are things <code>cases</code> wants to avoid. You can instead use <code>match</code> here and generalize <code>f n</code> \"explicitly\":</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">refl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or just <code>generalize</code> directly:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">generalize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 582901866,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1774993284
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Right, so either way, there's a generalization step that has to occur. What I was asking is then whether there's any reason the generalization step should not be done by an inversion tactic as needed, given that this is a pretty common pattern, and that the variables created by generalization in these scenarios aren't typically used directly?</p>",
        "id": 583167549,
        "sender_full_name": "Jonathan Chan",
        "timestamp": 1775095059
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One thing I'd like to know is what proof state Coq's inversion tactic ends up with when you do this; do you simply get an equation <code>f n = 0</code> in the proof state?</p>",
        "id": 583366401,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1775166671
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yep, try this <a href=\"https://jscoq.github.io/scratchpad.html\">online</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Coq\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">Example</span> <span class=\"n\">foo</span> <span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span> <span class=\"o\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">nat</span> <span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"n\">nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span> <span class=\"o\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">le</span> <span class=\"o\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">f</span> <span class=\"n\">n</span> <span class=\"o\">&lt;=</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">f</span> <span class=\"n\">n</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">.</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">Proof</span><span class=\"o\">.</span>\n  <span class=\"k\">inversion</span> <span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"o\">.</span>\n  <span class=\"kp\">reflexivity</span><span class=\"o\">.</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">Qed</span><span class=\"o\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(paste then click the down arrow button on the right a few times to step through the proof)</p>",
        "id": 583366985,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1775167034
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suppose something like this?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"inversion \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\" with\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ppSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">colGt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ident</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span>\n<span class=\"n\">elab_rules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inversion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">ids</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getMainGoal</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">withContext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fvar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getFVarId</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">var</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ids</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ids</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getD</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fvar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getType</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">whnf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">withApp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">matchConstInduct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fn</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throwTacticEx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`inversion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">m!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"major premise type is not an inductive type{indentExpr type}\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">induct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">us</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nparams</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">induct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">numParams</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gens</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GeneralizeArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">0.</span><span class=\"bp\">..</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">nparams</span><span class=\"bp\">...*</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">nparams</span><span class=\"bp\">...*</span><span class=\"o\">][</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ids</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">?.</span><span class=\"n\">getDM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">gens</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gens</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arg</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">hName?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getId</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span cl